        "original_id": "cf82e56e-b824-53a8-85e4-53489e565a14",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Tivolis Koncertsal, Tivoli Gardens, Copenhagen, Denmark, Klampenborg\n- Products: Tivoli Two\n- People: Duke Jordan\n- Organizations: SteepleChase\n- Concepts: amusement parks, live albums\n\nFacts:\n- Tivoli Gardens opened on 15 August 1843.\n- Tivoli Gardens is the second-oldest operating amusement park in the world after Dyrehavsbakken in nearby Klampenborg, Denmark.\n- Tivolis Koncertsal is a 1,660-capacity concert hall located at Tivoli Gardens in Copenhagen, Denmark.\n- Tivoli Two is a live album by Duke Jordan's Trio recorded at Tivolis Koncertsal.\n- Tivoli Two was first released on the Danish SteepleChase label in 1984.",
